From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:01:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Include stdlib.h for malloc and free in format.h

fmt::detail::allocator calls malloc and free, but format.h never
included <stdlib.h>; it relied on the C++ headers pulling it in. The
libc++ that ships with clang-r596125 (LLVM 22) trims those transitive
includes, so rootcanal's libbt-rootcanal (log.cc, hci/address.cc) failed
with "use of undeclared identifier 'malloc'". Upstream fmt 11.1 adds the
same include.

Change-Id: I0bc6e3ad2fe6e7ca2bb15b527ddf61085f9fb560
---
 include/fmt/format.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/fmt/format.h b/include/fmt/format.h
index ffe4fe0..0ecd5cc 100644
--- a/include/fmt/format.h
+++ b/include/fmt/format.h
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
 #  include <initializer_list>  // std::initializer_list
 #  include <limits>            // std::numeric_limits
 #  include <new>               // std::bad_alloc
+#  include <stdlib.h>          // malloc, free
 #  if defined(__GLIBCXX__) && !defined(_GLIBCXX_USE_DUAL_ABI)
 // Workaround for pre gcc 5 libstdc++.
 #    include <memory>  // std::allocator_traits
